{"agent":"bhq","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`scan_kilo` now compares `created < since * 1000` and evaluates `marker not in raw` in Python. A Kilo `part` row with `time_created` NULL or `data` NULL used to be dropped by SQL (`NULL >= ?` / `instr(NULL, ?) > 0` is unknown). Given that row, this comparison raises TypeError and aborts the whole override listing instead of skipping the row.","digest":"7a675038cd65db99","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:419","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:419"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`@cache` on `_kilo_question_parts` memoizes the empty tuple that `read_only_rows` returns for a locked, missing, or unreadable store. Given a transient lock on the first ask, every later `scan_kilo` in the same process still sees `()` after the database is readable, so valid harness approvals are dropped for the rest of the process. The same cache also freezes transcript bytes in `_lines`, so a file appended after the first scan is never re-read.","digest":"afcec821622d1b04","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:395","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:395"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression test asserts `len(reads) <= 1` and stubs `_dirs` to `[]`, so it never executes `_lines`/`scan`. Zero queries also satisfy `<= 1`. If `OV.rows` does not call the Kilo scanner, the test stays green on the unfixed per-ask re-read, and the state-R CPU path (every consumed ask still walking every cached line) is unmeasured and still unbounded.","digest":"f6312d91d910ac7e","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_approvals_audit_wire2.py:104","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_approvals_audit_wire2.py:104"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6256,"diff_sha":"2